<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gia Long Code</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1815">1815</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Hoàng Việt luật lệ, Hoang Viet luat le</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gia-long">Gia Long</a> Code, officially Hoàng Việt luật lệ, was the legal code of the Nguyen dynasty, promulgated by Emperor Gia Long in 1815. Closely modelled on the code of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a>, it replaced the Lê code and organised criminal, administrative and family law in about four hundred articles. It remained in force, with amendments, until the French colonial period.</p></div>
